From 0020000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: distsystem <dev@dist.systems>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-pci: reset-on-resume quirk for AMD Strix Halo xHCI

On the ASUS ProArt PX13 (AMD Strix Halo), s2idle resume intermittently
hangs for ~10 seconds with the on-APU xHCI controller (1022:1587):

  xhci_hcd 0000:c4:00.4: xHCI host not responding to stop endpoint command
  xhci_hcd 0000:c4:00.4: xHCI host controller not responding, assume dead
  xhci_hcd 0000:c4:00.4: HC died; cleaning up
  PM: resume of devices complete after 10424 msecs

The controller comes back from s2idle in a bad state and never
acknowledges the Stop Endpoint command. The command-timeout watchdog
(~5s) then fails to abort the command ring (~5s) and declares the host
dead, blocking the dpm_resume barrier for the full ~10s and freezing the
desktop before it thaws.

This is the same broken state-restore-on-resume already quirked for
earlier AMD APU xHCI controllers (Raven 0x15e0/0x15e1, Raven2 0x15e5).
Strix Halo 0x1587 is a new member of that family and is missing from the
quirk table. Reset the controller on resume instead of restoring its
state, exactly as done for Raven2 0x15e5 above; devices on it
re-enumerate (~1-2s) rather than the host dying.

Not yet upstream; same symptom tracked at FrameworkComputer
SoftwareFirmwareIssueTracker issue #163.

Signed-off-by: distsystem <dev@dist.systems>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
@@ -328,6 +328,15 @@
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_RESET_ON_RESUME;
 	}
 
+	/* AMD Strix Halo USB 3.1 xHCI (1022:1587) does not respond to the
+	 * Stop Endpoint command on s2idle resume; the controller comes back
+	 * in a bad state, the command times out and the host is declared
+	 * dead, stalling dpm_resume for ~10s. Reset the controller on resume
+	 * instead of restoring state (same fix as Raven2 0x15e5 above).
+	 */
+	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_AMD && pdev->device == 0x1587)
+		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_RESET_ON_RESUME;
+
 	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_AMD && pdev->device == 0x43f7)
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_DEFAULT_PM_RUNTIME_ALLOW;
 
